# ArcHive: the marketplace site at the root, the console under /console/, AskHive, the site copilot (/copilot-site/),
# and the MCP server over HTTP (/mcp). Caddy rereads this file only when it is recreated: deploy.sh does that.
# ArcHive over HTTPS, one origin (the browser's HPKE encryption needs a secure context).
# The certificate is obtained and renewed automatically by Caddy (Let's Encrypt, otherwise ZeroSSL).
# Caddy replaces any X-Forwarded-For sent by the client with the connection's real IP (no trusted proxy is declared):
# the API uses it for its per-IP rate limit.
#
# arc-hive.xyz (A records @ and www to 62.171.153.35) and archive.62-171-153-35.sslip.io serve the SAME site; the
# sslip.io address is the one the enclaves, the registrars, the operator scripts and the published links call, and the
# console's origin:
#  - the console (/console/) is built for the sslip.io address (build.sh, PUBLIC_URL), and its CSP would block its calls
#    from the other name, so /console/ on arc-hive.xyz redirects to sslip.io;
#  - the copilots (server and enclave; ALLOWED_ORIGINS is measured into the enclave image) accept the sslip.io origin,
#    so Caddy forwards requests from https://arc-hive.xyz (the same site, on the same server) under that origin;
#  - wallet signatures (EIP-4361: pairing, operator keys) are bound to sslip.io (the API's WEB_URL); on arc-hive.xyz the
#    site says so and links to the console.
#  Moving the primary name to arc-hive.xyz (PUBLIC_URL, WEB_URL, the enclaves' ALLOWED_ORIGINS) is part of the v3 cutover.
www.arc-hive.xyz {
	redir https://arc-hive.xyz{uri} permanent
}

archive.62-171-153-35.sslip.io, arc-hive.xyz {
	encode gzip

	@console_newname {
		host arc-hive.xyz
		path /console /console/*
	}
	redir @console_newname https://archive.62-171-153-35.sslip.io{uri} 302

	# Discovery for AI agents, answered by Caddy itself so that build.sh (rsync --delete into web/) never
	# removes it. /llms.txt (llmstxt.org): what ArcHive is, the MCP server, the public API, products and prices, how
	# payments are guarded. /.well-known/mcp-registry-auth: the public key of the HTTP domain proof for the official MCP
	# Registry (registry.modelcontextprotocol.io, name xyz.arc-hive/archive); its private key was deleted after the
	# publication. To publish an update: a new Ed25519 key, its record in the respond line below, mcp-publisher login http.
	handle /llms.txt {
		header Content-Type "text/plain; charset=utf-8"
		header Cache-Control "public, max-age=300"
		respond <<LLMS
			# ArcHive
			
			> Sealed machines, open market. ArcHive is a marketplace on Arc testnet where AI agents and apps pay per use in USDC for compute on Intel TDX enclaves that a contract on Arc verifies on-chain. Operators earn by renting out their machines, authors by publishing services. Built for UBC 2026. Testnet only: no real funds move.
			
			A contract on Arc admits an enclave only once Intel's signature on its quote (DCAP) and the fingerprint of the exact image it runs check out. USDC moves only against a receipt an admitted enclave signed, and a proven lie costs the operator its USDC bond.
			
			## Connect an AI agent (MCP)
			
			- Claude Code, one line: `claude mcp add --transport http archive https://arc-hive.xyz/mcp`
			- [MCP server](https://arc-hive.xyz/mcp): Streamable HTTP, stateless, 16 tools, no key. The tools read products, enclaves, prices, sessions, bounties and on-chain activity, check a receipt, and prepare unsigned actions: nothing is signed or sent, the user signs in their own wallet.
			- MCP Registry name: xyz.arc-hive/archive
			
			## Public read API (JSON, no key)
			
			- [/api/products](https://arc-hive.xyz/api/products): each product's on-chain parameters (price and unit, shares, settlement contract, minimum bond, exposure cap, state)
			- [/api/enclaves](https://arc-hive.xyz/api/enclaves): the enclaves Arc admitted, with operator, product, key and validity window
			- [/api/pricing?productId=1&units=1000](https://arc-hive.xyz/api/pricing?productId=1&units=1000): the cost of a use, units times the product's price
			
			## Products and prices (Arc testnet, USDC)
			
			- Product 1, private AI by prepaid session: 0.10 USDC per 1,000 tokens. Deposit once into SessionPay; price and model are locked at opening, settlements never pay more than the deposit, the rest is refunded at close.
			- Product 3, private AI per call (x402): 0.01 USDC per call, one EIP-3009 signature per call, no gas for the agent. Call it through our TypeScript SDK (packages/sdk in the repository), which checks the enclave's key on Arc before it encrypts the request.
			- AskHive (product 4), the attested copilot on the site: free.
			- Also on the network: the Sealed Bounty (products 2 and 7), a USDC pool that pays out only for an exploit a sealed enclave replayed.
			
			## How payments are guarded
			
			- Admitted enclaves only: the SDK encrypts (HPKE) only to a key Arc registered for the product and active now; settlement pays only a signer that was active for the product at the receipt's anchor block.
			- One payment, one call (x402): the authorization is for the exact price, to the X402Settler contract only, and its nonce commits to the sealed request; the SDK signs nothing above the agent's maxAmount.
			- Session budget (product 1): settlements are capped by the deposit; what is not spent is refunded.
			- Operator bond: an operator's enclaves can release at most half of its bond in any 24 hours, and at most 10 USDC per product on testnet; a proven lie forfeits the bond.
			- Split: the operator whose enclave served the request earns 95 % of each paid call or session, the network keeps 5 %.
			
			## Links
			
			- [Site](https://arc-hive.xyz)
			- [The Doc](https://arc-hive.xyz/doc.html): how Arc checks every machine, every proof linked
			- [Services, prices and shares](https://arc-hive.xyz/service.html)
			- [Source code, MIT license](https://github.com/JeanBaptisteDurand/UBC_2026)
			- [Arc testnet explorer](https://explorer.testnet.arc.io)
			LLMS 200
	}
	handle /.well-known/mcp-registry-auth {
		header Content-Type "text/plain; charset=utf-8"
		header Cache-Control "no-cache"
		respond "v=MCPv1; k=ed25519; p=NogVE0ahCqFYdbJse2/8wBhg0LudcxSabtmKvl01Eig=" 200
	}

	# read API, machine pairing, test mode (the API also caps every route at 64 KiB)
	handle_path /api/* {
		request_body {
			max_size 256KB
		}
		reverse_proxy api:8809
	}

	# the console copilot
	handle_path /copilot/* {
		request_body {
			max_size 512KB
		}
		reverse_proxy copilot:8808 {
			# requests from arc-hive.xyz are forwarded under the sslip.io origin, the one the copilots accept (see the header)
			header_up Origin ^https://arc-hive\.xyz$ https://archive.62-171-153-35.sslip.io
			transport http {
				read_timeout 180s
			}
		}
	}

	# Arc testnet's public RPC: the same target as the front's development proxy (frontend/vite.config.ts: /arc-rpc to
	# https://rpc.testnet.arc.io). For state proofs, a gateway to an Arc archive node (deploy/arc-node/rpc-gate.mjs,
	# host.docker.internal:8810) can take its place.
	@arcrpc path /arc-rpc /arc-rpc/*
	handle @arcrpc {
		uri strip_prefix /arc-rpc
		request_body {
			max_size 128KB
		}
		reverse_proxy https://rpc.testnet.arc.io {
			header_up Host {upstream_hostport}
			transport http {
				read_timeout 30s
			}
		}
	}

	# AskHive, the site copilot ("site" surface: it guides the visitor through the site's pages)
	handle_path /copilot-site/* {
		request_body {
			max_size 512KB
		}
		reverse_proxy copilot-site:8808 {
			# requests from arc-hive.xyz are forwarded under the sslip.io origin, the one the copilots accept (see the header)
			header_up Origin ^https://arc-hive\.xyz$ https://archive.62-171-153-35.sslip.io
			transport http {
				read_timeout 180s
			}
		}
	}

	# MCP server over HTTP (Streamable HTTP, stateless): other agents (Claude, Cursor…) use ArcHive's tools
	@mcp path /mcp /mcp/*
	handle @mcp {
		request_body {
			max_size 64KB
		}
		reverse_proxy mcp:8812
	}

	# site + enclave proxy (/enclave/inference/, /enclave/bounty/…): the web container's nginx
	handle {
		# the copilot's enclave (/enclave/copilot-site/, behind nginx) checks the origin too
		reverse_proxy web:80 {
			# requests from arc-hive.xyz are forwarded under the sslip.io origin, the one the copilots accept (see the header)
			header_up Origin ^https://arc-hive\.xyz$ https://archive.62-171-153-35.sslip.io
		}
	}

	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		X-Frame-Options "DENY"
		Permissions-Policy "camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()"
		# Scripts: only the site's own (no inline script, no third party); 'wasm-unsafe-eval' for three.js's meshopt
		# decoder (the site's 3D scene): it compiles WebAssembly, not JavaScript (eval stays forbidden). Connections: the
		# site itself (API, copilots, enclave proxy), Arc's RPC and explorer, enclaves at Phala and behind a cloudflared
		# tunnel (registering a machine: the browser reads its /attest), the Sepolia and Base Sepolia RPCs and Circle's
		# Iris sandbox for CCTP transfers, WalletConnect, Coinbase Wallet and RainbowKit's ENS resolver.
		# Inline styles allowed (RainbowKit injects its themes); https images (wallet icons); never framed.
		Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://iris-api-sandbox.circle.com https://rpc.testnet.arc.io https://explorer.testnet.arc.io https://*.phala.network https://*.trycloudflare.com https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com https://base-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com https://*.walletconnect.com wss://*.walletconnect.com https://*.walletconnect.org wss://*.walletconnect.org https://enhanced-provider.rainbow.me https://api.wallet.coinbase.com wss://www.walletlink.org; frame-src https://verify.walletconnect.com https://verify.walletconnect.org; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'"
		# no software or version announced (nginx's or Caddy's Server header, the proxy's Via)
		-Server
		-Via
	}
}
